WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.834
More now on the breaking

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.302
news in the Washington, D.C.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:02.702
region.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.070
F-16 fighter jets

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.871
scrambled shortly

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.073
before a small plane crashed in Virginia.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.576
The aircraft created a sonic boom

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.244
that a large number of people hurt.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.046
Here's a look from one person's

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.547
security camera.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.056
And CNN aviation

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.090
correspondent Pete Montaigne

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:24.657
joins us now.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:26.393
Pete, you have new information on this.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.694
What can you tell us?

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.963
We're just getting a statement now, Jim,

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:30.730
from Norwood,

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.531
and I want to read it to you.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.033
This is from CNN's Hayley Brzezinski

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.035
from Tyndall Air Force Base in Florida.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.770
NORAD's says F-16 fighter

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.203
aircraft

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:39.506
responded to an unresponsive

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.774
Cessna Citation jet

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.108
that is a very large business jet

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:44.677
sits between seven and 11 people.

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:46.179
This happened earlier today

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.414
in northern Virginia,

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.415
nor at aircraft,

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:48.948
this statement

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.550
says, were authorized to travel

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.018
at supersonic speeds,

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.054
which would explain the sonic boom

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:54.687
that was heard

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.589
far and wide from Annapolis, Maryland,

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.223
to Leesburg,

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:59.059
Virginia, all the way down to Manassas

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.360
and Quantico.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.594
Nor Ed says in this statement

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.762
during this event,

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.298
the nor had aircraft also use flares,

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.233
which may have been visible to the public

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.401
in an attempt to draw attention

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.636
to the pilot.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:10.570
Flares were deployed

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.572
with the highest regard for safety

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.807
of the intercepted aircraft

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.608
and people on the ground.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.976
The plane was intercepted

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.412
around three 20 Eastern Time.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.780
Today

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.549
and the pilot was unresponsive

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:23.416
subsequently

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.251
subsequently crashed near the George

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.720
Washington National Forest in Virginia.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.123
I'm also hearing from a source familiar

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.558
with this investigation

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:32.959
that four people

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:33.793
were on board

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.529
this airplane pilot unresponsive.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.398
That plane overshot

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.600
its initial destination in New York

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.470
by about 315 miles.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.672
You can see the track there on flight

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.340
tracking site FlightAware.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.976
The plane took off from Tennessee

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.644
and then went northeast

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.579
bound over

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:54.647
northern Virginia, over the eastern shore

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.249
of Maryland, Delaware,

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.350
southern New Jersey,

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.885
and then turned inbound

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.253
for a Long Island there,

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:03.556
then proceeded to fly southwest bound

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.626
and through the layer and layer and layer

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:08.027
of restricted airspace

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.496
around Washington, D.C.,

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.997
it's known as the flight restricted zone

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.133
and the special flight rules area.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.367
That apparently is

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:16.102
what triggered this intercept.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.103
To me right now,

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.238
I can tell you as a pilot

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.239
and a flight instructor, of the

00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:19.806
sounds like

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:21.474
the Payne Stewart incident,

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.643
you may remember back in the nineties

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.445
when the pro golfer was on board

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.546
his Learjet

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.314
and that airplane had a sudden loss

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.916
of cabin pressurized ocean.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:30.850
The crew, as well

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.852
as the passengers on board passed out

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.654
because of the high altitude,

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:35.355
the high altitude

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.590
air outside, not breathable inside.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.025
Therefore, fighter jets

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:40.793
were scrambled in a similar incident

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:42.729
to try and intercept that airplane.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.164
Ultimately, that plane crashed.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.031
So we know,

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.966
at least from the Virginia State Police,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.067
that they are still searching

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.102
for the wreckage here

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.971
in a very rural area of Virginia.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.374
But the latest information from North Add

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.976
is that the pilot was unresponsive

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.112
and that fighter jets were scrambled

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.314
and they were okayed to go supersonic.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.483
So all of the things are lining up here.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.318
It was not just a sonic boom

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.085
that we heard,

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.854
not just a military pilot

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:09.656
who eked through the sound barrier

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.557
by accident.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:12.458
This was something that was intentional.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.493
And they were trying to

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:14.928
get to this airplane

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.996
with the pilot who was not responding.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.566
So it does not seem at least right now

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:20.767
that this was something

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.602
that was intentional, not like something

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.270
it was a terroristic act.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.104
This is something that

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.973
where the pilot was not responding

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.575
and they had to send fighter jets

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:30.710
to rule out some possibilities here, Jim.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:31.711
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.413
And if we can

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:34.881
I don't know if we can show that graphic

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.049
one more time for our viewers,

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:37.483
because I think that was very helpful

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.418
earlier in this hour,

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.152
we were talking about

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:39.686
whether or not

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:40.620
the plane just took off

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.589
from northeast tip of Tennessee

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:43.156
and then crashed

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.490
in the mountains of Virginia.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.859
That is that that can

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.361
underline why it was so alarming

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.862
for military officials, U.S.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.130
Air Force officials,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:51.931
for that plane

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.633
to go all the way up to Long Island

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:55.835
and then turn around and come back down.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:57.870
That's very strange.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.739
That's very unusual to see something like

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:00.206
that happen.

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.942
What do you think?

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.677
And that is something

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.646
that still needs to be explained here.

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.248
But if there was a rapid loss

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:10.283
of cabin pressurization in this airplane

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:11.851
and the pilots and passengers

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:13.086
passed out because of the

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.153
thin air outside,

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:14.520
they were up

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.321
relatively high,

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:16.589
as initially saw between

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:18.391
30 and 40,000 feet.

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.726
You can't maintain consciousness

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:20.426
for very long.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.294
You have to put oxygen

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:23.696
masks on very, very quickly

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:25.832
so you can see the path there initially.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:28.201
So the bottom right corner of your screen

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.402
to the sorry bottom

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:30.203
left corner of your screen,

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:30.837
to the top right

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:31.671
corner of your screen,

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.339
that was the initial path.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.340
And you can see that

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.608
the plane went around.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.710
What would be the DC area there

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.711
and then

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.813
flew over Long Island, Islip

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:43.182
there and turned back to the southwest.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.150
So it's possible

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.252
the airplane was on automatic pilot

00:04:46.252 --> 00:04:47.287
that it may have just sort of

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.888
continued flying on a heading

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.723
after it reached the destination.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.792
You can see the green track there

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:55.061
after it looks around on Long Island.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:55.928
There goes

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.264
right over the District of Columbia,

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:00.333
right over Washington, D.C.

00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.668
So you can tell that

00:05:01.668 --> 00:05:04.003
this was very clearly cause for alarm.

